  "notes": [
    "Addresses copied verbatim from bgd-labs/aave-address-book src/AaveV4Ethereum.sol. RE-VERIFY each byte-for-byte against that raw source (or Etherscan) before generating a production merkle root.",
    "Users/integrators (and the BoringVault) call the SPOKE contracts. Each Spoke draws liquidity from a Liquidity Hub internally, so the Hub is NOT called directly by the vault and needs no merkle leaves. Whitelist Spoke targets, not Hubs.",
    "IMPORTANT: an Aave V4 reserve is identified by a uint256 reserveId (Spoke-local index), NOT by the asset token address. A decoder can only pin ADDRESS arguments, so the merkle root CANNOT restrict which reserveId an action touches — only onBehalfOf/user/positionManager are pinned. Constrain the market by choosing WHICH Spoke target (and off-chain which reserveId) each leaf authorizes.",
    "Decoder: src/base/DecodersAndSanitizers/Protocols/AaveV4DecoderAndSanitizer.sol (also merged into nextgen/FullDecoderAndSanitizer.sol)."
  ],
